WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.967
A useful analysis usually asks more than one question.

00:00:03.967 --> 00:00:10.682
In this continuation of the product sales example, we can calculate month-to-month growth for a product and compare

00:00:10.682 --> 00:00:13.500
variability across products.

00:00:14.094 --> 00:00:22.196
Growth tells us how values change over time, while standard deviation can help us compare how stable or variable

00:00:22.196 --> 00:00:24.516
different product sales patterns are.

00:00:24.516 --> 00:00:29.521
When interpreting the result, avoid focusing only on the code.

00:00:29.521 --> 00:00:32.176
Ask what the calculation means.

00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:39.991
A product with high average sales but very high variability may behave differently from a product with slightly lower

00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:42.038
but much more stable sales.
